---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Intent & Proof | Measurable Customer Acquisition Systems"
	description="Intent & Proof builds SEO, landing page and lead generation systems for service businesses."
>
	<section class="hero">
		<div class="hero-inner">
			<div class="eyebrow">WELCOME TO INTENT &amp; PROOF</div>

			<h1>Learn how to turn search intent into qualified leads.</h1>

			<p class="hero-subtitle">
				Practical guides, templates and systems for service businesses that want cleaner SEO, better landing pages and campaigns that can actually be measured.
			</p>

			<div class="proof-box">
				<div class="proof-avatar">IP</div>
				<div>
					<p class="proof-quote">“Most local businesses do not need more traffic first. They need a cleaner path from search intent to tracked enquiries.”</p>
					<p class="proof-name">Intent &amp; Proof</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<form class="audit-box">
				<input type="email" placeholder="Email Address" aria-label="Email Address" />
				<button type="submit">Try It</button>
			</form>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="section-head">
			<div>
				<h2>Latest Growth Guides</h2>
				<p>Practical articles on SEO, landing pages, tracking and lead generation.</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="card-grid">
			<article class="card">
				<div class="card-kicker">Local SEO</div>
				<h3>How service businesses can build city pages that actually convert.</h3>
				<p>Not decorative SEO pages. Real landing assets with search intent, proof, CTAs and internal links.</p>
			</article>

			<article class="card">
				<div class="card-kicker">Landing Pages</div>
				<h3>The anatomy of a high-converting service landing page.</h3>
				<p>Hero, proof, offer, objections, local trust signals and conversion tracking. Wildly enough, structure matters.</p>
			</article>

			<article class="card">
				<div class="card-kicker">Tracking</div>
				<h3>Why most small business campaigns fail before the first click.</h3>
				<p>No clean events, no attribution, no decision system. Just budget being released into the atmosphere.</p>
			</article>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
